---
import { ExternalLink, Info, Ruler, Trophy, Wallet } from "lucide-react";
import AppLayout from "../layouts/AppLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import PageNav from "../components/PageNav.astro";
import {
  budgetPoints,
  budgetTiers,
  caseStudies,
  spaceBenchmarks,
  spaceSources,
} from "../data/proposal";

const findings = [
  {
    icon: Trophy,
    title: "Field access",
    body: "Nearly every top team practices on a full field regularly, but few have one inside their school. Those that do usually got it through a district facility funded by a bond or state grant.",
  },
  {
    icon: Ruler,
    title: "Floor space",
    body: "A full field with room around it needs about 2,800 sq ft, and a working shop about 3,000 sq ft. Single-school facilities at top programs run 6,500–7,800 sq ft. The field sets the size, whatever the enrollment.",
  },
  {
    icon: Wallet,
    title: "Budgets",
    body: "Competitive district teams typically spend $50,000–80,000 a year, and world-level programs $150,000 or more. Most of it goes to registration and travel, not the robot.",
  },
];

const link =
  "inline-flex items-center gap-1 underline decoration-foreground/30 underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary hover:decoration-primary";
---

<AppLayout title="Research | Garage robotics lab proposal">
  <PageHeader
    slug="research"
    title="How successful teams practice"
    image="04-field-from-east-aisle"
  >
    We looked at where top FRC teams build and drive, how much space they use,
    and what they spend.
  </PageHeader>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What we found</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      {
        findings.map((f) => (
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-card p-5 shadow-xs ring-1 ring-foreground/10">
            <f.icon className="size-5 text-primary" aria-hidden="true" />
            <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold">{f.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">{f.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <div
      class="mt-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl bg-muted p-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground"
    >
      <Info
        className="mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-foreground"
        aria-hidden="true"
      />
      <p>
        No public dataset tracks FRC team facilities, so these findings come
        from published examples, not a representative sample. We plan to survey
        teams across the U.S. to fill the gap.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y bg-card">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Case studies</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-muted-foreground">
        Teams get field time in one of three ways. Mentors note that practicing
        on a full field is something most teams can't do in-house.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 space-y-12">
        {
          caseStudies.map((group) => (
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">{group.model}</h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">{group.summary}</p>
              <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
                {group.teams.map((t) => (
                  <article class="flex flex-col rounded-xl bg-background p-5 ring-1 ring-foreground/10">
                    <h4 class="font-semibold">
                      {t.name}
                      {t.place && (
                        <span class="ml-2 text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">
                          {t.place}
                        </span>
                      )}
                    </h4>
                    <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                      {t.body}
                    </p>
                    <p class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                      {t.sources.map((s) => (
                        <a href={s.url} class={link} rel="noopener">
                          {s.label}
                          <ExternalLink className="size-3" aria-hidden="true" />
                        </a>
                      ))}
                    </p>
                  </article>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-16 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How much space a field needs</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl ring-1 ring-foreground/10">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[28rem] text-left text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-muted text-foreground">
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Space</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-semibold"
                >Sq ft</th
              >
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Basis</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y bg-card">
            {
              spaceBenchmarks.map((r) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">
                    {r.space}
                  </th>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums">
                    {r.sqft}
                  </td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">{r.basis}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
        Chief Delphi threads:{" "}
        {
          spaceSources.map((s, i) => (
            <>
              {i > 0 && " · "}
              <a href={s.url} class={link} rel="noopener">
                {s.label}
              </a>
            </>
          ))
        }
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How our plan compares</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        <li>
          The garage bay is about 60 × 48 ft, roughly the 2,800 sq ft a full
          field with driver stations needs.
        </li>
        <li>
          Mentors generally treat a little over half a field as the practical
          minimum. A half field fails for games that score at opposite ends. The
          3/4-scale field in Option B clears that bar.
        </li>
        <li>
          Across the garage, cage, Room 6, and Room 3, the lab totals about
          4,300 sq ft, below the 6,500–7,800 sq ft purpose-built facilities but
          inside a building the district already owns.
        </li>
        <li>
          FRC carpet comes in 15 ft rolls, and the border needs extra width on
          each side of the 27 ft field, so carpet layout should be checked on
          site.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y bg-card">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What teams spend</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]">
        <dl class="space-y-3">
          {
            budgetTiers.map((b) => (
              <div class="rounded-xl bg-background p-4 ring-1 ring-foreground/10">
                <dt class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">{b.tier}</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight tabular-nums">
                  {b.amount}
                </dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl ring-1 ring-foreground/10">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[32rem] text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-muted text-foreground">
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Team</th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Figure</th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Notes</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y bg-background">
              {
                budgetPoints.map((r) => (
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">
                      <a href={r.url} class={link} rel="noopener">
                        {r.who}
                      </a>
                    </th>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums">
                      {r.figure}
                    </td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">{r.note}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-16 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What this means for Melrose</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        <li>
          Red Hawk Robotics already raises money at the level of a competitive
          district team. Compared with peers, the gap is space, not funding.
        </li>
        <li>
          The closest models (Davis, Madera, and Martin County) each got a field
          through a district facility. This proposal reaches a similar result by
          reusing a building the district already owns.
        </li>
        <li>
          A field on site avoids rent, which some teams pay at about $30,000 a
          year, and cuts trips to shared fields such as WPI's. It also gives the
          district a place for scrimmages and younger FIRST programs.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What we don't know yet</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        <li>
          What share of teams have a field in their school, and how space varies
          with enrollment. Our planned survey of U.S. teams will ask both.
        </li>
        <li>
          Massachusetts funding routes for school facilities, such as state
          school building or CTE grants.
        </li>
        <li>
          Facility details for several other top teams, including 254, 2056,
          4414, and 1538.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PageNav slug="research" />
</AppLayout>
